{
  "brief_rationale": "The trajectory preserved the acute respiratory safety chain: the doctor identified persistent SpO2 below 90 as respiratory failure risk, pushed immediate EMS/ED care, maintained monitored oxygen/ventilatory management, and repeatedly addressed refusal without treating alertness or transient improvement as reassuring. The doctor also gave executable family roles, escalation thresholds, patient-facing scripts, and later ICU goals-of-care communication guidance with responsible-service handoff. Multiple high-order points were actively completed, especially real-world constraint navigation, misconception correction, and verification of oxygen/blood-gas context. No responsibility-chain error or important non-chain defect is supported by the visible evidence, so the deterministic grade is 5.",
  "closure_assessment": {
